,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\/#faq-question-1750165346081\",\"name\":\"What is keyword difficulty?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"<a href=\\\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-difficulty\/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noreferrer noopener\\\">Keyword difficulty <\/a>(KD) measures the difficulty level to rank a specific keyword based on competition. Higher difficulty means more effort is required to rank.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\/#faq-question-1750165356238\",\"position\":7,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\/#faq-question-1750165356238\",\"name\":\"Should I target high-volume or low-competition keywords?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"There should be a balance between the two. Long-tail, low-competition keywords are ideal for newer sites, while high-volume keywords are targeted by established and big brands as their authority grows.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\/#faq-question-1750165378110\",\"position\":8,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\/#faq-question-1750165378110\",\"name\":\"How often should I update keyword research?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"You must revise keyword research and strategy every few months, especially when you launch a new product, there is a new trend in your niche, and there is a shift in your business goals.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\/#faq-question-1750165387918\",\"position\":9,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\